Jonadab the Unsightly One <jonadab.theunsightlyone@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> If I wanted to be really evil, I'd suggest an even higher-threat
> member of the class, R, Disintegrator, a creature who just plain
> outright destroys one item from your inventory each time he
> hits you, starting with armor (armor that's not covered by other
> armor going first), followed if he continues hitting you after
> you're armorless by wielded items next, followed then by
> whatever else you might happen to be carrying.  If he should
> ever happen to hit you when you have *nothing* in your
> inventory, you die, unless you have disintegration resistance.

But that's not how things usually work in NetHack. Inventory items
don't protect you if they are only carried besides some exceptional
magic items.

The disintegrator should work the same as a breath of disintegration,
so you'd only have 2 strikes (large shield and body armor) or 3 if you
also are wearing an amulet of life saving.

> Anything you throw at him would disintegrate, of course, so
> the only ways to harm him would be in melee (which lets
> him destroy stuff) or with wands or spells.  Oh, and he would
> probably be resistant to stoning, just to make it fair.

Stonsing-resistant makes sense. After all the corpse should
disintegrate when touching the disintegrator.

Maybe its HP should get reduced when it gets hit by an object as
somehow model the conservation of energy and matter-antimatter
reaction that happens. More physical exact would be to reduce its
weight until it reaches 0. But IIRC monsters (not monster corpses)
don't have weight in NetHack.

